{
  "id": 529437813,
  "iid": 26414,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "SMPP: Use 32-bit integer for PDU length to prevent truncation",
  "description": "According to SMPP v3.4 and v5.0 specifications (section 4.1.1), the command_length field is a 4-octet integer value. The dissector read the length using tvb_get_ntohl() but assigned it to a uint16_t variable, causing truncation for PDU lengths exceeding 65535 bytes.\n\nThis caused the dissector to either prematurely abort dissection when the lower 16 bits wrapped to zero or desynchronize from PDU boundaries and parse payload contents as headers.\n\nChange pdu_len to uint32_t to match the 4-byte wire representation.",
  "state": "merged",
  "created_at": "2026-09-08T12:46:29.869Z",
